WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.660
A, B, and C all happen at the same time, right?&nbsp;
Well, they appear to occur in a different order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:12.240
depending on the observer's reference frame.&nbsp;
This is a key concept in Albert Einstein's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.640
Special Theory of Relativity in which it's&nbsp;
impossible to say if two events occurred at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:23.640
the same time if those events are separated&nbsp;
in space. In real life, a car crash in New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:29.580
York and another in Prague appear to occur at the&nbsp;
same time to an observer on Earth. However, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:34.860
will appear to have occurred at different times&nbsp;
to someone flying between New York and Prague.

